    "user": "U0A5EGHRLQY",
    "text": "Hi team, I was trying to upgrade to this release but getting following error:\n```Error: UPGRADE FAILED: execution error at (olake/templates/olake-worker/serviceaccount.yaml:4:26): Fusion is not supported when global.logFileStorageMode is s3; set fusion.enabled to false or use nfs```\nHave we removed support for fusion when `logFileStorageMode` is s3?\nHere is the addition I did in my current values file along with setting `global.logFileStorageMode=s3`:\n```\ns3LogFileStorage:\n  bucket: \"\u0026lt;my-bucket\u0026gt;\"\n  prefix: \"olake/logs\"\n  region: \"ap-south-1\"\n  minio:\n    enabled: false\n  external:\n    role:\n      enabled: true\n      annotations:\n        \u003chttp://eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn|eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn\u003e: \"\u0026lt;arn\u0026gt;\"```\nPS: The role ARN I am using here is same as `global.jobServiceAccount.annotations` ARN which is used for s3 authentication for iceberg writes",
